<title>BRAZIL: BRAZIL PARANAGUA JULY SUGAR EXPORTS WELL ABOVE '96.</title>
<headline>BRAZIL PARANAGUA JULY SUGAR EXPORTS WELL ABOVE '96.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sugar shipments out of Brazil's port of Paranagua in July totaled 236,785 tonnes, up from 183,350 tonnes in the same month last year, the port authority said.</p>
<p>Of this year's total, 101,847 tonnes were bagged sugar and 134,938 tonnes bulk. In July last year, the split was 91,666 tonnes bagged and 91,684 tonnes bulk.</p>
<p>The July 1997 shipments compare with 155,374 tonnes in June and bring sugar shipments from Paranagua since the start of this year's center-south harvest in May to 483,146 tonnes against 240,228 tonnes during May to July 1996.</p>
<p>The higher shipments are due to deliveries of 260,000 long tons of Paranagua raws against the New York May contract which were to be completed by the middle of July.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
